meta {
  name: 6. Create POSTGIS DataSink
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datasets/:dataSetId/datasinks
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  dataSetId: {{pgDataSetId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "dataSinkType": "POSTGIS",
    "configuration": {
      "tableName": "saga_geo_observations",
      "element": "{{pgTargetModelUrn}}"
    }
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.body && res.body.id) {
    bru.setVar('pgDataSinkId', res.body.id);
  }
}

tests {
  test("DataSink created", function() {
    const status = res.getStatus();
    // 201=created. This collection assumes a clean DB per run (CI uses an ephemeral stack); a 409
    // would mean a previous run leaked — fail loudly rather than carry a stale id downstream.
    expect(status).to.equal(201);
  });

  test("Has POSTGIS type", function() {
    if (res.getStatus() === 201) {
      expect(res.body.dataSinkType).to.equal('POSTGIS');
    }
  });
}

docs {
  **PostGIS saga step 6** — Prerequisites: dataset created (step 5), target version released (step 3b).

  Creates a POSTGIS DataSink nested under the dataset. The sink is associated with the dataset via the path `dataSetId` (the input DTO's `dataSetId` is `@JsonIgnore`/path-derived, never sent in the body). It is **not** linked via a pipeline id — the pipeline (step 7) declares this sink in its `dataSinkIds`, which is an optional convenience link; the saga discovers sinks by dataset id regardless.

  The `configuration` map carries the two POSTGIS-required fields validated by the backend: `tableName` (non-blank) and `element` (the CORE URN of an existing model in the registry). The adapter derives the sink table's columns — including `geo` as `GEOMETRY(POINT,4326)` — from that version's JSON Schema.

  **Expected Response:** 201 Created, body contains `id` and `dataSinkType: "POSTGIS"`. 409 if a previous run already created it.

  **Post-condition:** Save `pgDataSinkId` from `body.id` (referenced by the pipeline in step 7 and deleted in cleanup step 13).

  **System Impact:**

  | Layer | Effect |
  |---|---|
  | Backend | DataSink record created in `portal_backend` DB, FK `dataset_id` → this dataset |
  | Config Adapter | — (table is provisioned only when the DATASET_CREATE saga runs in step 9) |
  | External System | — |
}
